'''Jannah''', formerly known as '''TZ-1719''', was a [[human]] [[Gender|female]] and former [[First Order]] [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] who lived on [[Kef Bir]] after deserting. She was a freedom fighter who, by the [[time]] of the [[First Order-Resistance War]], led a [[Company 77|tribe]] of [[Soldier|warriors]] on the [[ocean]] [[moon]]. Sometime later she became an ally of the Resistance. She used an [[Jannah's energy bow|energy bow]]. [[Finn]] was pleasantly surprised by her story, as prior to meeting her he was unaware that there were others like him who had defected from the First Order. Jannah and her crew assisted Finn and the Resistance in taking down the [[Sith Eternal]]'s [[fleet]], the [[Final Order]], during the [[Battle of Exegol]].

==Biography==
===Training with the First Order===
{{Quote|You were First Order?''"''<br />''"''Not by choice.|Finn and Jannah|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
The [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who would take on the name Jannah<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> was [[Reproduction|born]] between [[12 ABY|12]] and [[15 ABY]].<ref name="Jannah birth" /> At some point, she was taken from her family at a young age by the [[First Order]], within which she was trained by [[Captain]] [[Phasma]] as a [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]]<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> under the designation TZ-1719.<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> In the First Order, she developed skills in archery,<ref name="TROS Junior Novel" /> turning her into someone who was second-to-none among [[energy bow]] archers.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> She was assigned to [[Company 77]].<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> Jannah served the First Order as a dutiful stormtrooper for many [[Standard year|years]].<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>

===Defection===
{{Quote|We laid our weapons down.''"''<br />''"''All of you?''"''<br />''"''The whole company.|Jannah and Finn|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:Company77-TheRiseOfSkywalker3.png|thumb|right|300px|TZ-1719 removes her helmet as Company 77 refuses to fire on civilians.]]
Years before [[35 ABY]],<ref name="AnsettDate">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' establishes that [[Company 77]] began their life on [[Kef Bir]] sometime after the [[Battle of Ansett Island]] and that the [[company]] has lived on Kef Bir for [[Standard year|years]] by the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], the events of which occur in [[35 ABY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Therefore, the Battle of Ansett Island must have been years before 35 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]].</ref> TZ-1719 and the rest of Company 77 were deployed into a [[Battle of Ansett Island|battle]] for [[Ansett Island]], a body of land in<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> the [[Ansett system]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="GalaxyMap">[[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]]</ref><ref name="Planetnamia">{{Planetnamia|other=Ansett Island|system=the [[Ansett system]]}}</ref> During the battle, Company 77 was ordered to fire on civilians<ref name="Episode IX" /> as a massacre,<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> but TZ-1719 and the rest of the company all refused, lying down their weapons and then defecting from the First Order. According to another stormtrooper defector, [[Finn]], it was [[the Force]] that spoke to TZ-1719 and her fellow stormtroopers to convince them to rebel.<ref name="Episode IX" /> 

Through her strength as a leader and warrior, Z-1719&mdash;who adopted the name Jannah after her escape&mdash;found herself rising to<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> de facto<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> leadership amongst the company, which eventually settled down on one of the moons of [[Endor (planet)|Endor]], [[Kef Bir]],<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> in [[Exile (punishment)|exile]].<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> Through [[comlink]] communication, she maintained a degree of contact with [[The galaxy|the wider galaxy]] via an underground community of technology salvagers, who shared advice and designs. Among that group was [[Babu Frik]], a [[droidsmith]] who worked for the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]],<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" /> although Jannah herself remained unfamiliar with him.<ref name="Episode IX" /> Frik, meanwhile, knew of them as a collection of [[orbak]] riders.<ref name="Rise of SkywalkerVD" />

===Encounter with the Resistance===
{{Quote|We picked up a transmission from someone named Babu Frik.''"''<br />''"''Babu Frik? Oh, he's one of my oldest friends.''"''<br />''"''He said you'd come. He said you were the last hope.|Jannah and C-3PO|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:FinnCompany77.png|thumb|left|275px|Jannah and her tribe meet the Resistance.]]
In [[35 ABY]], [[Resistance]] operatives [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], [[Finn]], [[Poe Dameron]], [[Chewbacca]], [[BB-8]], [[C-3PO]], and [[D-O]] arrived on Kef Bir in search of the [[Darth Sidious|Emperor's]] [[wayfinder]]. Being informed by Babu Frik about their mission, Jannah agreed to help them. Jannah helped Finn and Dameron fixed the badly crashed ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''. While fixing the ''Falcon'', Jannah handed Finn a gadget which Finn recognized as a piece used by the First Order. Realizing that he had a history with the First Order, Jannah revealed she and her whole crew were once stormtroopers who refused to fire on civilians much like what Finn did during the [[Attack on Tuanul]]. Jannah explained how it didn't even feel like a decision but more like an instinct to which Finn replied that it was [[the Force]], which probably brought him to her. Shocked by this, Jannah said that Finn said this like it is real to which he replied it is. Just then BB-8 interrupted them and told them that Rey was not with them. Leaving the ''Falcon'', Finn realized in horror that Rey had impatiently took one of the [[sea skiff]]s and headed to the [[Death Star ruins|ruins]] of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]]. Seeing the danger, Jannah offered Finn another sea skiff to help Rey. Using the sea skiff, Jannah and Finn explored the corridors of the wreckage in search of Rey. Hearing lightsabers clash, they ran out to trench and saw her fighting [[Supreme Leader]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]. Trying to interfere, Finn called out her name but was pushed back by the Force. As Finn tried to interfere again, Jannah told him that they couldn't follow them.<ref name="Episode IX" />

===Joining the Resistance===
Stranded on the ruins, Finn called Poe and told them to come rescue them. Jannah along with Company 77 boarded the ''Millennium Falcon'' and flew back to the [[Resistance base (Ajan Kloss)|Resistance base]] on [[Ajan Kloss]] where they learned of [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia]]'s death. Poe was named [[General]] of Resistance. Just then, they were informed that [[Kijimi]] had been completely [[Destruction of Kijimi|destroyed]] by the [[Sith Eternal]]. With some advice from [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] and Finn as his co-general, Poe devised a plan to take out the [[Xyston-class Star Destroyer|''Xyston''-class Star Destroyers]] of the [[Final Order]]. As Lando and Chewbacca used the ''Falcon'' rallied up any free worlds to help aid them, Jannah and her crew gathered up their [[orbak]]s and boarded the ''[[Fortitude]]'' and headed to [[Exegol]] thanks to Rey using Kylo Ren's wayfinder to transmit the map to the Resistance.<ref name="Episode IX" />

===Battle of Exegol===
{{Quote|The nav signal's coming from that command ship. That's our drop zone.''"''<br />''"''How do you know?''"''<br />''"''A feeling.|Finn and Jannah|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:ExegolLandingTeam.png|thumb|right|250px|Jannah riding an orbak on the side of the ''Steadfast''.]]
Arriving on Exegol, the Resistance was immediately attacked by the [[Sith Eternal military|Sith Eternal forces]]. While the [[Exegol air team]] tried to protect the [[Exegol landing team|ground team]], the fleet's navigation tower suddenly switched off. Knowing that the disabling the tower was the only way to prevent the Sith Star Destroyers from leaving Exegol, the Resistance opted retreat. However, Finn sensed from the Force that the navigation signal was coming from the [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] [[Steadfast (Resurgent-class)|''Steadfast'']]. Jannah asked how he knew to which Finn replied a "feeling." Landing on the hull of the ship, Jannah, Finn, and the rest of the Resistance team used the orbaks to ride across the ship as they were confronted by [[Sith trooper]]s. Jannah threw and detonator to distract the troopers and gave them enough time for BB-8 to open the hatch, during which she shot down a [[Sith Jetpack Trooper]]. When BB-8 got the hatch open, they threw down a [[bandolier]] of grenades which destroyed the hatch and temporarily shut down the navigation signal.<ref name="Episode IX" />

When everybody was retreating, Finn realized that the Sith Eternal was planning on rebooting the system. He decided to stay and destroy the Resurgent Star Destroyer. Jannah chose to stay with him and help him destroy it. Turning one of the destroyer's [[turbolaser]]s on its [[Bridge (starship)|bridge]], Jannah and Finn witnessed the arrival of a [[Citizens' Fleet]] from across the galaxy commanded by Lando to help them, the arrival caused a great turn of tide in the battle. However, down below in the Sith Citadel, [[Darth]] Sidious, now fully revived by absorbing Rey and Ben Solo's [[Force dyad]], used a vast amount of Force lightning at the fleet, temporarily disabling them. Rey, guided by the spirit of past [[Jedi]], used both the [[Skywalker lightsaber]] and [[Leia's lightsaber]] to destroy the [[Sith Lord]]. With Sidious dead and the Force lightning stopped, Jannah and Finn were able to use the turbolaser to destroy the command ship, killing [[Allegiant General]] [[Enric Pryde]]. The ''Steadfast'' began falling toward the surface with Jannah and Finn still on it, but they were saved by Lando and Chewbacca onboard the ''Millennium Falcon''. With the Sith fleet destroyed and Sidious dead, the Resistance and their civilian fleet won the battle and retreated back to Ajan Kloss.<ref name="Episode IX" />

===Aftermath===
{{Quote|Where are you from, General?''"''<br />''"''The Gold System. Well, what about you, kid?''"''<br />''"''Oh. I don't know.''"''<br />''"''Well, let's find out.|Jannah and Lando Calrissian|<ref name="Episode IX" />}}
[[File:JannahAndLandoCalrissian_Ep9.png|thumb|left|250px|Jannah and Lando Calrissian after the Battle of Exegol.]]
Back on Ajan Kloss, the Resistance and their allies celebrated their victory and the defeat of Sidious and the Sith Eternal. Seeing Lando, Jannah sat beside him and asked him where he was from, to which he replied the [[Gold system]]. Turning around, Lando asked Jannah where she was from with the latter saying she did not know. Smiling, Lando offered to help Jannah travel across the [[galaxy]] to help find her home.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Skills and abilities==
[[File:Jannah-TRoSOCE.png|thumb|right|250px|Jannah was skilled with the energy bow she constructed.]]
Jannah was an extremely competent [[engineer]] who created her energy bow with recycled parts from [[blaster rifle]]s. She possessed a natural ability to make her comrades trust and follow her.<ref name="Galactic Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Galactic Guide]]''</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|All I can really say is the original group is going on this epic, epic adventure together, and Jannah crosses paths with them.|Naomi Ackie|<ref name="13 things">{{SW|url=news/swcc-2019-13-things-we-learned-from-the-star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker-panel|text=SWCC 2019: 13 Things We Learned from the ''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'' Panel}}</ref>}}
Jannah was a character portrayed by [[Naomi Ackie]] in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], the final installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[sequel trilogy]].<ref name="Episode IX" /> Jannah's name and appearance were first revealed during the "''Star Wars'': Episode IX" panel at [[Celebration Chicago]] on [[April 12]], 2019.<ref name="Episode IX panel">{{SWYouTube|RnhiLZOprZE|Star Wars: Episode IX Panel &#124; Star Wars Celebration Chicago 2019}}</ref> For her character, Ackie was required to train for seven months to learn horseback riding.<ref>{{WebCite|url=https://www.gamesradar.com/star-wars-the-rise-of-skywalker-naomi-ackie-jannah-interview|text=Exclusive: Naomi Ackie teases Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker role: "Jannah shows up at the right time"|author=Farley, Jordan|date=2019-10-15|archivedate=20200107084756}}</ref>

